  {
   "id": "consent-managers",
   "where": "background.js CONSENT_MANAGER_HOSTS",
   "relaxes": "Consent manager banner and choice saving hosts load even though annoyance and tracker lists name them.",
   "reason": "With the banner blocked no refusal is ever saved and a site treats the reader as undecided. Auto reject answers the banner instead. Where auto reject is on, OneTrust's stub is answered locally (surrogates/onetrust.js), so OneTrust's own files load only where it is off or paused, or where a site hosts OneTrust itself. Their analytics hosts are not listed and stay blocked.",
   "evidence": "Round 5 consent runs, 2026-11-20: refusals saved on 17 of 22 sites (DuckDuckGo 3, plain Edge 0). OneTrust local answer, 2026-11-21: requests to OneTrust on 20 OneTrust sites fell from 211 to 12, refusal saved on 17.",
   "tests": [
    "tools/test-feed-shared-platforms.js",
    "tools/test-onetrust-answer.js"
   ],
